v26.07 (2026-07-31)
-------------------
- Replace awk {n,} interval expression in usage() with a portable equivalent for mawk compatibility.
- Quote $1 in R.zsh's set_r_path to prevent word-splitting on paths containing spaces.
- Quote $1 in java.zsh's set_java_path and $JAVA_HOME in its PATH/CLASSPATH exports to prevent word-splitting on paths containing spaces.
- Pass paths as positional parameters in install_dotzsh.sh's zsh -c zcompile calls to prevent word-splitting.
- Stop installation and return an error when a critical command fails.
- Install ~/.zshrc without sudo so it stays owned by the invoking user instead of root.
- Accept nosudo as the sole installation argument instead of treating it as a target directory name.
- Honor a preset ZSH_ROOT in the installed .zshrc, so the search for a configuration tree is skipped at shell startup.
- Keep .zshrc exiting with status zero when ~/.zshrc_local is absent, so the first prompt no longer reports a failed command.
- Correct the README customization section to state that a user-level tree replaces the system-wide one instead of merging with it.
- Document how ZSH_ROOT is resolved, the .zshrc_local hook, and that --uninstall keeps .zshrc_local.
- Clarify install_dotzsh.sh usage/help and README to note that --uninstall always targets the default path and ignores a custom target_path.
- Remove the obsolete README step that copies dot_zshrc by hand, which the installer already does.
- Honor the nosudo argument for install_dotzsh.sh --uninstall, which was ignored after the option was documented as --uninstall [nosudo].
- Check required commands before uninstalling, as is already done before installing.
- Accept --no-sudo and -n as aliases for the installer's existing nosudo argument.
- Accept the installer's no-sudo flag before the target path, which was previously discarded when the flag came first.

